{{#> layouts/base head-sub-title="Modules" page-title="Simple Java Mail Modules" }}

	{{#*inline "html-head-block"}}
<meta name="Description" content="List of all Simple Java Mail modules and what 3rd party dependencies they bring">
	{{/inline}}

	{{#*inline "header-block"}}
		{{> includes/header topic="modules" }}
	{{/inline}}

  {{#*inline "body-block"}}
  <section>
    <p class="wide">
      Start with <code>simple-java-mail</code>. Add an optional module only when you need pooled batch delivery, authenticated SOCKS, DKIM, S/MIME,
      Outlook conversion, command-line use, Spring integration, or Karaf support.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <div class="view">
      <p>
        The main <code class="inline language-text">simple-java-mail</code> dependency already includes the core module. Add any optional feature modules
        alongside it as you need them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Integration modules such as Spring already depend on the main library, so you do not need to declare it twice. Feature modules can be combined.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: 1em">The main core dependencies are:</p>
      <ul class="indent">
        <li><code>jakarta.mail:jakarta.mail-api</code> — the standard mail API</li>
        <li><code>org.eclipse.angus:angus-mail</code> — the Jakarta Mail implementation</li>
        <li><code>com.sanctionco.jmail:jmail</code> — address validation</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Use the published POM on Maven Central as the authoritative list of transitive dependencies for the current release.</p>
      <p style="margin-top: 1em">
        As of 9.0.0, the <code class="inline language-text">simple-java-mail</code> and <code class="inline language-text">core-module</code> jars include
        Java module descriptors. Modular applications can require
        <code class="inline language-java">org.simplejavamail</code> directly.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="side">
	    <img data-src="../../assets/module_architecture.png"
	         data-src-webp="../../assets/module_architecture.png.webp"
			 alt="Simple Java Mail module overview">
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2 id="batch-module" class="with-back-to-top">Batch and clustering support</h2>

  <section>
    <p>
      To enable support for async / batch mode sending using connection pooling, and clustering (see <a href="configuration.html#section-batch-and-clustering">Configuration</a>),
		include the following library:
    </p>
    <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.simplejavamail&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;batch-module&lt;/artifactId&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</code></pre>
    <p>
      This adds the following 3rd party dependencies:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a class="indent" href="https://github.com/simple-java-mail/smtp-connection-pool">simple-java-mail:smtp-connection-pool</a></li>
    </ul>
	  <p class="wide">
      The module sends work asynchronously and adds configurable worker threads and SMTP connection pools. See
      <a href="configuration.html#section-batch-and-clustering">configuration</a> for details.
    </p>
	  <p class="wide">
		  A live connection pool keeps the JVM running. Call <code>mailer.shutdownConnectionPool()</code> during application shutdown for every mailer that
		  owns a pool, including each mailer in a cluster.
	  </p>
  </section>

  <h2 id="authenticated-socks-module" class="with-back-to-top">Authenticated (SOCKS) proxy support</h2>

  <section>
    <p>
      To enable support for authenticated SOCKS proxy servers (see <a href="features.html#section-proxy">Features</a>),
      include the following library:
    </p>
    <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.simplejavamail&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;authenticated-socks-module&lt;/artifactId&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</code></pre>
    <p>
      This adds no additional 3rd party dependencies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <h2 id="outlook-module" class="with-back-to-top">Outlook support</h2>

  <section>
    <p>
      To enable support for parsing Outlook messages (see <a href="features.html#section-converting">Features</a>),
      include the following library:
    </p>
    <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.simplejavamail&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;outlook-module&lt;/artifactId&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</code></pre>
    <p>
      This adds the following 3rd party dependencies:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a class="indent" href="https://github.com/EsotericSoftware/kryo">com.esotericsoftware:kryo</a></li>
      <li><a class="indent" href="https://github.com/magro/kryo-serializers">de.javakaffee:kryo-serializers</a></li>
      <li><a class="indent" href="https://github.com/bbottema/outlook-message-parser">org.simplejavamail:outlook-message-parser</a></li>
      <li>Of which that last in turn adds:</li>
      <li><a class="indent" href="https://poi.apache.org/">org.apache.poi:poi</a></li>
      <li><a class="indent" href="https://poi.apache.org/">org.apache.poi:poi-scratchpad</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <h2 id="dkim-module" class="with-back-to-top">DKIM support</h2>

  <section>
    <p>
      To enable support for DKIM signing (see <a href="security.html#section-sending-dkim">Features</a>),
      include the following library:
    </p>
    <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.simplejavamail&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;dkim-module&lt;/artifactId&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</code></pre>
    <p>
      This adds the following 3rd party dependencies:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a class="indent" href="https://github.com/markenwerk/java-utils-mail-dkim">net.markenwerk:utils-mail-dkim</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <h2 id="smime-module" class="with-back-to-top">S/MIME support</h2>

  <section>
    <p>
      To enable support for sending and reading <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S/MIME">S/MIME</a>
      signed / encrypted email, (see <a href="security.html#section-sending-smime">Features</a>),
      include the following library:
    </p>
    <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.simplejavamail&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;smime-module&lt;/artifactId&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</code></pre>
    <p>
      This adds the following 3rd party dependencies:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a class="indent" href="https://github.com/markenwerk/java-utils-mail-smime">net.markenwerk:utils-mail-smime</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <h2 id="cli-module" class="with-back-to-top">CLI support</h2>

  <section>
	  <p class="wide">
		  Normally, you would not need the CLI module on the class path, unless you wish to invoke the
		  <code class="language-text">static void main</code> method from Java (see also <a href="cli.html#navigation">how to use CLI</a>).
		  To do so, include the following module:
	  </p>
    <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.simplejavamail&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;cli-module&lt;/artifactId&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</code></pre>
    <p>
      This adds the following 3rd party dependencies:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a class="indent" href="https://github.com/remkop/picocli">info.picocli:picocli</a></li>
      <li><a class="indent" href="https://github.com/dnault/therapi-runtime-javadoc">com.github.therapi:therapi-runtime-javadoc</a></li>
      <li><a class="indent" href="https://github.com/bbottema/java-reflection">com.github.bbottema:java-reflection</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="wide">
      <strong>Note:</strong> Simple Java Mail core has a 'provided' dependency on <em>com.github.therapi:therapi-runtime-javadoc-scribe</em>
      which burns Javadoc into Simple Java Mail at compile time. This cannot be made optional. If this is a real concern, an option
      could be to provide two versions of Simple Java Mail: one with embedded Javadoc and one without (incompatible with the Cli Module).
      This is currently not in scope.
    </p>
  </section>

  <h2 id="spring-module" class="with-back-to-top">Spring support</h2>

  <section>
	  <p>
		  To enable Spring support (see <a href="configuration.html#section-spring-support">Configuration</a>), include the following module:
	  </p>
	  <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.simplejavamail&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;spring-module&lt;/artifactId&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</code></pre>
	  <p>
		  This adds the Spring core dependency, which is assumed to be on the classpath already.
	  </p>
  </section>

  <h2 id="karaf-module" class="with-back-to-top">Apache Karaf support</h2>

  <section>
	  <p>
		  To enable Apache Karaf support, include the following module:
	  </p>
	  <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.simplejavamail&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;karaf-module&lt;/artifactId&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</code></pre>
	  <p>
		  NOTE: the artifact is currently temporarily named: 'simplejavamail-karaf-feature'.
		  It will be named correctly in the next release.
	  </p>
  </section>
  {{/inline}}

